desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Unirest Http Request"
	title_zh: "Unirest Http Request"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-unirest-http-request"
	risk: "cleartext-transmission"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `unirest-http-request` (problem-based-packs/insecure-transport/java-stdlib/unirest-http-request.yaml).
Original message: Checks for requests sent via Unirest to http:// URLS. This is dangerous because the server is attempting to connect to a website that does not encrypt traffic with TLS. Instead, send requests only to https:// URLS.
CWE: CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information
References:
- https://kong.github.io/unirest-java/#requests
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Preferred replacement: https://
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.java": <<<POS
Unirest.get("http://example.com")
POS
	"safefile://pos.java": <<<NEG
Unirest.get("https://example.com")
NEG
)

${*.java}.pattern_regex(/(?:Unirest\.(?:get|post)\(\s*["\'][hH][tT][tT][pP]:\/\/[^"\']*["\']\s*\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Unirest Http Request",
	title_zh: "Unirest Http Request",
	message: "Unirest Http Request detected.",
}
